<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salzkammergut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Salzkammergut is an Alpine lake district in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-austria">Upper Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>, named after the salt mines and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> chamber that administered them. Salt had been mined at Hallstatt since prehistoric times, and under the Habsburgs the region was a closely controlled crown estate whose output was a major source of revenue. Hallstatt and its surroundings are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salzkammergut.jpg" alt="Salzkammergut" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hallstatt_-_Zentrum_.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
